(D) THE TRUNCATION MARGIN IS A NAMED CONSTANT:  1 - log(pi^2/4)
====================================================================================================
  M >= log(pi v/2) is needed;  M = log(2Q/pi) + 1 and v <= Q give margin 1 - log(pi^2/4) = 0.096835
  pole separation: spacing 1/v >= 1/Q must exceed 2 e^{-M}/pi = 1/(Q e) -- true, factor e.
  direct check:       Q        M     min over q<=Q of [min_t Phi^(M) - floor]
