SUMMARY
====================================================================================================
  coset identity + Fourier proof   : CONFIRMED
  q = 2: my closed form for the minimiser was FALSIFIED (0.4993 at 5/6 claimed; true
         minimum 0.494530 at L = 0.7908).  The hand-provable two-branch bound
         holds: 0.346574 and 0.370081, both >= (1/2) log 2 = 0.346574 : CONFIRMED
  major-arc radius  L_0 = 0.4528 < 1, so ||theta|| >= 1/N is a safe minor arc
  truncation margin  1 - log(pi^2/4) = 0.096835
  derived error bound dominates    : YES
  positive control on the scan     : passed
